title: A sudden scream.
new-page: true
  
There was a scream. You felt the crowd surge in movement, it pressed into your back. A woman stumbled back into you, you gripped her, she turned, her eyes wide and mouth open, she shook herself out your grasp, she stared at you like you were a monster. 

You looked up, the shrill, an alien sound, barbaric, inhuman, animalistic! Police whistles, stitching panic amongst the people, the scream of metal, a police armoured car, was it the same you saw in Wedding? It lurched itself onto the street.

The side hatch of the car opened, a dark square mouth appeared. There was a gleaming noise, a belt of brass reflecting on the sun, you swore to God that you were about to die. 

But instead, it was something else. Water, it came out, first, the water was sprayed into the crowd, it flushed everyone soaked and damp. 

You fell on the pavement, your hand catching you, your clothes were damped, you felt you weighed perhaps triple what you normally do. You covered your face and eyes, your hair falling in front. Instinctively you shouted, “Erika!” She did not answer you

The water’s gushing flood ended, you stood up, quickly, you looked around, you shouted again, “Erika!” You felt a hand, soaked, touch your neck, it was wet, “I’m here, Karl!” Her voice shouted, it calmed you.

But it did not stop you, you felt your arm wrap around her like an iron bar, you almost pulled her down, trying to shield her head with your own. “The baby!”

You screamed, Erika shouted “Where’s Hannah? Hannah!” Erika looked around, trying to see through you, around you. The crowd was blooming all around you, unthinking panic. There was trampling of the mass, a child’s hoop rolled perfectly upright, but in the forest of fleeing legs, it was delicate, trampled, vanquished. 
  
You looked forward, you saw that Pushcart man, nearer to the front, being savaged. Besides him, there was a woman, she had bags of groceries, she too was being brutalised. 
  
The Social Democratic Police were pushing into the crowd, hurting all those who stood in their path. On Erika, your grip lessened, she tried to wrap hers around you, but you stepped too far too quickly, she tumbled to the ground.
